==================================================================
DAY 40 - PART B: LAB
Back up and restore etcd, then upgrade the cluster
Time: 120 minutes
==================================================================

All commands on cp1 unless stated. Snapshot your VMs first!


STEP 1: Install etcdctl/etcdutl matching your etcd
--------------------------------------------------
k get pod -n kube-system -l component=etcd -o jsonpath='{.items[0].spec.containers[0].image}{"\n"}'
  -> e.g. registry.k8s.io/etcd:3.5.21-0  => ETCD_VER=v3.5.21
ETCD_VER=v3.5.21
curl -L https://github.com/etcd-io/etcd/releases/download/${ETCD_VER}/etcd-${ETCD_VER}-linux-amd64.tar.gz -o /tmp/etcd.tgz
tar xzf /tmp/etcd.tgz -C /tmp
sudo install /tmp/etcd-${ETCD_VER}-linux-amd64/etcdctl /tmp/etcd-${ETCD_VER}-linux-amd64/etcdutl /usr/local/bin/
etcdctl version

Helper:
cat >> ~/.bashrc <<'EOF'
alias e='sudo ETCDCTL_API=3 etcdctl --endpoints=https://127.0.0.1:2379 --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key'
EOF
source ~/.bashrc
e endpoint health ; e member list -w table


STEP 2: Create known state and take a snapshot
----------------------------------------------
k create ns before-backup
k create deploy keepme -n before-backup --image=nginx:1.27 --replicas=2
sudo mkdir -p /backup
e snapshot save /backup/etcd-$(date +%F).db
sudo etcdutl snapshot status /backup/etcd-$(date +%F).db -w table
sudo tar czf /backup/pki-$(date +%F).tgz /etc/kubernetes/pki
ls -lh /backup


STEP 3: Make changes after the backup
-------------------------------------
k delete ns before-backup                     # "accidental" delete
k create ns after-backup                      # new work
k get ns


STEP 4: Restore
---------------
SNAP=/backup/etcd-$(date +%F).db
sudo mkdir -p /root/manifests-stopped
sudo mv /etc/kubernetes/manifests/{kube-apiserver,etcd}.yaml /root/manifests-stopped/
sleep 20 ; sudo crictl ps | grep -E "etcd|apiserver"     # gone

sudo etcdutl snapshot restore $SNAP --data-dir /var/lib/etcd-restore
sudo sed -i 's#path: /var/lib/etcd$#path: /var/lib/etcd-restore#' /root/manifests-stopped/etcd.yaml
sudo grep -n "etcd-restore" /root/manifests-stopped/etcd.yaml   # hostPath changed

sudo mv /root/manifests-stopped/{etcd,kube-apiserver}.yaml /etc/kubernetes/manifests/
sudo systemctl restart kubelet
sleep 60
k get ns                   # before-backup is back, after-backup is gone
k get deploy -n before-backup

(If kubectl hangs: sudo crictl ps -a | grep etcd ; sudo crictl logs <id>)


STEP 5: Plan the upgrade
------------------------
Current version:
  k get nodes
Switch the repo to the next minor (example v1.33 -> v1.34):

Ubuntu:
  sudo sed -i 's/v1.33/v1.34/' /etc/apt/sources.list.d/kubernetes.list
  sudo apt-get update
  sudo apt-cache madison kubeadm | head -3
  sudo apt-mark unhold kubeadm && sudo apt-get install -y kubeadm='1.34.*' && sudo apt-mark hold kubeadm
RHEL/Rocky:
  sudo sed -i 's/v1.33/v1.34/g' /etc/yum.repos.d/kubernetes.repo
  sudo dnf install -y kubeadm-'1.34.*' --disableexcludes=kubernetes

kubeadm version
sudo kubeadm upgrade plan        # read it: target versions, components


STEP 6: Upgrade the control plane
---------------------------------
sudo kubeadm upgrade apply v1.34.x -y     # use the exact version from plan
k get pods -n kube-system -o wide         # new static pod images

k drain cp1 --ignore-daemonsets
Ubuntu:
  sudo apt-mark unhold kubelet kubectl && sudo apt-get install -y kubelet='1.34.*' kubectl='1.34.*' && sudo apt-mark hold kubelet kubectl
RHEL:
  sudo dnf install -y kubelet-'1.34.*' kubectl-'1.34.*' --disableexcludes=kubernetes
sudo systemctl daemon-reload && sudo systemctl restart kubelet
k uncordon cp1
k get nodes                     # cp1 shows v1.34.x


STEP 7: Upgrade each worker (one at a time)
-------------------------------------------
On worker1: switch repo, upgrade kubeadm (same as Step 5), then
  sudo kubeadm upgrade node
On cp1:
  k drain worker1 --ignore-daemonsets --delete-emptydir-data
On worker1: upgrade kubelet + kubectl (as in Step 6), then
  sudo systemctl daemon-reload && sudo systemctl restart kubelet
On cp1:
  k uncordon worker1
  k get nodes
Repeat for worker2. Keep a curl loop running against the NodePort
service from Day 39 during the worker upgrades: does it stay up?


STEP 8: Verify and record
-------------------------
k get nodes -o wide
k version
sudo kubeadm certs check-expiration     # renewed by upgrade apply
k get pods -A | grep -v Running

Write a runbook ~/k8s-journey/kubeadm/upgrade-runbook.md with every
command, then commit.
